{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/783635-clarification-on-cat-fox-magic","id":783635,"title":"Clarification on Cat/Fox Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-10T13:44:33-08:00","id":783635,"title":"Clarification on Cat/Fox Magic","content":"Hey folks, I've got a nearly fresh new Bastet character and I'm a little confused about learning Gifts and Cat Magic. On page 85 of Changing Breeds, it says that Bastet learn Gifts from other werecats or by stealing them from other werecreatures. On page 208, under the merit Cat/Fox Magic, it says Bastet can learn hedge magic. I'm not too interested since hedge magic seems complicated and anemic compared to gifts, potentially a huge waste of xp. However, it also says they can mimic Gifts and rites from other werecreatures.<br /> <br /> So, when they refer to stealing Gifts is this a reference to Cat Magic or do they differentiate 'stealing' from 'mimicking'? To me, stealing seems like they're watching a Garou or whoever and studying when they use Gifts to learn their secrets. Mimicking seems more like a spell that has a similar effect as a Gift but isn't one. For example, if my Bastet wants 360 degree vision, does he track down and study an Ananasi until he learns the Many Eyes gift or is he at home with a spellbook designing a spell that just uses Many Eyes as an easy mechanic to plug-in?<br /> <br /> Edit: another clue in the Bubasti Magic sidebar on page 76. The option is to allow Bubasti to create spells that mimic Gifts from other werecreatures. It mentions the Cat Magic merit as a &quot;more robust system&quot;<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10160-concolitanos","user":"Concolitanos","date":". 12-10-2015, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10160-concolitanos","name":"Concolitanos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T04:17:18-08:00","id":784050,"title":"","content":"Stealing gifts and Cat/Fox Magic are different. The first is just an alternative way that they are known for acquiring gifts by watching others from afar. Its handled more like learning gifts from another person in that it requires a lot of trial and error and I think their is a limitation on how high of a gift you can learn in that manor. The second is Sorcery, in that sidebar you mentioned I remember there being specific paths that the Bubasti actually use and I am pretty sure the Merit tells you to reference the Sorcerer book from the Revised material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T07:40:02-08:00","id":784158,"title":"","content":"Derzhuzad is right. Don't quote me on this, but I think Bastet Breedbook stated that you can not steal gifts higher than level 3, and you can't take gifts that are nonsensical for a Bastet to use, for example if it requires poison fangs or fins your character obviously doesn't have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T13:15:17-08:00","id":792329,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this was a rule in the book or just a rule in the MES Addendum, but I also know that in the LARP I'm a part of, to swipe a gift, you need to be able to see the gift in action - a gift that's visible (like Faerie Fire) is fine, but something subtle or that doesn't produce visible results (i.e. Body Mastery) can't generally be copied. This may only be an addendum rule as I said, but it's a good house rule to follow, IMO - not only do you need to be able to see it to guess at how it works, you need to be able to see it to know it's actually magic you can copy.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Cat Magic is different - it's the paths of magic used by sorcerers and other static mages. It's definitely expensive, but the idea is that their natures allow them to do strange things beyond just work with spirits to achieve effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}